    <section class="snap-section rd-sec rd-ez" id="arbeitsverstaendnis" data-index="1">
      <div class="about-band offers-band"></div>
      <div class="rd-inner">
        <div class="rd-eyebrow">Systemic Therapy &amp; Counseling</div>
        <div class="rd-cols">
          <div class="rd-clamp rd-col rd-text c1"><h2>The systemic view: seeing people in their contexts</h2><p>Systemic therapy and counseling widens the focus from the individual to their relationships and life circumstances. How we experience the world is strongly shaped by our experiences with important attachment figures and by the environments we move in.</p><p>Systemic approaches make it possible to bring couples, families or other people involved into the conversation, beyond the one-to-one setting. In individual sessions, we talk about your relationships with important people and the circumstances that matter for your concerns.</p><button class="rd-readmore" type="button" aria-expanded="false"><span class="faq-toggle"></span><span class="rd-readmore-t">Read more</span></button></div>
          <div class="rd-clamp rd-col rd-text c2"><h2>My professional perspective: patterns as attempts to solve a problem</h2><p>Unpleasant states and distressing behaviors are usually attempts to solve a problem. They arose in stressful situations and earlier relationships, served a protective function at the time, and today tend to run automatically under tension, often with unwanted side effects.</p><p>In a supportive space, I help you notice such patterns consciously and explore the needs and themes connected with them. This can bring clarity and a new sense of fit in how you communicate and relate to others. Alongside accepting what cannot be changed, you can widen your room for action and build more well-being.</p><button class="rd-readmore" type="button" aria-expanded="false"><span class="faq-toggle"></span><span class="rd-readmore-t">Read more</span></button></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="snap-section rd-sec rd-tint rd-ez" id="arbeitsweise" data-index="2">
      <div class="about-band offers-band"></div>
      <div class="rd-inner">
        <div class="rd-eyebrow">My approach</div>
        <div class="rd-cols">
          <div class="rd-clamp rd-col rd-text c1"><h2>Outside impulses for new perspectives</h2><p>We all have blind spots, because most of our inner processes run unconsciously. Feedback from trusted people and a professional outside perspective can make them visible and open the way for development.</p><p>I offer observations, questions and suggestions that you are free to examine, take up or set aside. In our shared process, we take the time you need to notice mindfully what feels right for you and which changes you want to work toward.</p><button class="rd-readmore" type="button" aria-expanded="false"><span class="faq-toggle"></span><span class="rd-readmore-t">Read more</span></button></div>
          <div class="rd-col rd-text c2"><h2>Approaches and methods in my work</h2>
            <div class="rd-chipgroup">
              <span class="rd-chipgroup-label">Approaches</span>
              <div class="rd-chips">
                <span class="rd-chip">systemic-constructivist</span>
                <span class="rd-chip">growth-oriented</span>
                <span class="rd-chip">hypnosystemic</span>
                <span class="rd-chip is-key">solution-focused</span>
                <span class="rd-chip is-key">short-term</span>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="rd-chipgroup">
              <span class="rd-chipgroup-label">Methods as needed and depending on your concern</span>
              <div class="rd-chips">
                <span class="rd-chip">inner parts work</span>
                <span class="rd-chip">body-oriented</span>
                <span class="rd-chip">imagery work</span>
                <span class="rd-chip">mindfulness-based</span>
              </div>
            </div>
            <p>Starting from your goals, we develop helpful perspectives, preferred ways of experiencing things and concrete next steps. We meet for as many sessions as make sense for your concerns.</p></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

