    <section class="snap-section rd-sec rd-tint rd-faq" id="faq" data-index="4">
      <div class="about-band offers-band"></div>
      <div class="rd-inner">
        <div class="rd-eyebrow">Systemic Therapy &amp; Counseling</div>
        <h2 class="rd-h2">Frequently asked questions</h2>
        <div class="rd-faq-grid">
          <div class="rd-faq-list">
            <div class="rd-faq-item is-active">
              <button class="rd-faq-q" aria-expanded="true"><span class="rd-num">01</span><span class="rd-q">How does working together begin?</span><span class="faq-toggle"></span></button>
              <div class="rd-faq-a"><div class="rd-faq-a-inner"><p>It begins with a free, no-obligation initial contact by phone or online by video. In about 20 minutes, we get to know each other and clarify the practicalities.</p><p>The first session follows. We clarify what brings you here and whether it feels right to work together. It is a regular session, charged at the usual rate.</p></div></div>
            </div>
            <div class="rd-faq-item">
              <button class="rd-faq-q" aria-expanded="false"><span class="rd-num">02</span><span class="rd-q">How long is a session, and how often do we meet?</span><span class="faq-toggle"></span></button>
              <div class="rd-faq-a"><div class="rd-faq-a-inner"><div class="faq-facts">
                  <div class="faq-fact"><span>Individual</span><strong>from 60 min.</strong></div>
                  <div class="faq-fact"><span>Two or more people</span><strong>from 90 min.</strong></div>
                  <div class="faq-fact"><span>Interval</span><strong>2–4 weeks</strong></div>
                  <div class="faq-fact"><span>Often helpful</span><strong>4–12 sessions</strong></div>
                </div>
                <p>Individual sessions start at 60 minutes; if you wish, we can agree on longer ones, for example 75 or 90 minutes. Sessions for two or more people start at 90 minutes, and here too we can agree on longer sessions, for example 105 or 120 minutes.</p><p>How many sessions you attend overall depends on your themes and needs. I often work in a brief, solution-oriented way: we meet only as often as is meaningful and necessary for your concerns. For deeper processes of change, 4 to 12 sessions are, in my experience, helpful.</p><p>We set the interval between sessions according to what works for you; it is usually between two and four weeks. Some people prefer very different rhythms, and a lot is possible. We agree on what suits you at the end of the first session and adjust it along the way.</p></div></div>
            </div>
            <div class="rd-faq-item">
              <button class="rd-faq-q" aria-expanded="false"><span class="rd-num">03</span><span class="rd-q">Do sessions also take place online?</span><span class="faq-toggle"></span></button>
              <div class="rd-faq-a"><div class="rd-faq-a-inner"><p>Sessions take place in Berlin-Moabit (INSA-Berlin · Alt-Moabit 91b) or online by video, in German or English.</p></div></div>
            </div>
            <div class="rd-faq-item">
              <button class="rd-faq-q" aria-expanded="false"><span class="rd-num">04</span><span class="rd-q">What costs can I expect?</span><span class="faq-toggle"></span></button>
              <div class="rd-faq-a"><div class="rd-faq-a-inner"><p>The rate is 150 euros per 60 minutes. Details on session lengths, invoicing and cancellation are on the costs page.</p><a class="rd-faq-link" href="{{ '/en/systemische-therapie/kosten/' | url }}">All details on costs, invoicing and cancellation<span class="rd-chev"></span></a></div></div>
            </div>
            <div class="rd-faq-item">
              <button class="rd-faq-q" aria-expanded="false"><span class="rd-num">05</span><span class="rd-q">Do you offer psychotherapy, and will health insurance cover the costs?</span><span class="faq-toggle"></span></button>
              <div class="rd-faq-a"><div class="rd-faq-a-inner"><p>No. My services are expressly not psychotherapy in the clinical sense under the German Psychotherapists Act (Psychotherapeutengesetz) or the Alternative Practitioners Act (Heilpraktikergesetz), but services outside the so-called remit of medical treatment (&ldquo;Heilauftrag&rdquo;). My work is based on recognized further training in Systemic Therapy &amp; Counseling (DGSF), Coaching (DGSv) and Supervision (DGSv/SG). I do not hold a state license as a psychotherapist (Approbation).</p><p>That is why my services are self-pay, and I bill you directly. Statutory and private health insurers do not reimburse them.</p></div></div>
            </div>
            <div class="rd-faq-item" id="faq-krise">
              <button class="rd-faq-q" aria-expanded="false"><span class="rd-num">06</span><span class="rd-q">Where can I turn in an acute mental health crisis?</span><span class="faq-toggle"></span></button>
              <div class="rd-faq-a"><div class="rd-faq-a-inner"><p>My services do not replace emergency care. If you are in an acute crisis, feel that you or others are at risk, or no longer know what to do, please get help immediately:</p>
                <div class="krise-btns">
                  <a class="krise-btn krise-btn-out" href="tel:+49303906310"><strong><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M22 16.92v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.18 2 19.79 19.79 0 0 1-8.63-3.07 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6 19.79 19.79 0 0 1-3.07-8.67A2 2 0 0 1 4.11 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.72c.127.96.361 1.903.7 2.81a2 2 0 0 1-.45 2.11L8.09 9.91a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.27-1.27a2 2 0 0 1 2.11-.45c.907.339 1.85.573 2.81.7A2 2 0 0 1 22 16.92z"/></svg>030 390 63 10</strong><span>Berliner Krisendienst · around the clock</span></a>
                  <a class="krise-btn krise-btn-fill" href="tel:112"><strong><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M22 16.92v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.18 2 19.79 19.79 0 0 1-8.63-3.07 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6 19.79 19.79 0 0 1-3.07-8.67A2 2 0 0 1 4.11 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.72c.127.96.361 1.903.7 2.81a2 2 0 0 1-.45 2.11L8.09 9.91a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.27-1.27a2 2 0 0 1 2.11-.45c.907.339 1.85.573 2.81.7A2 2 0 0 1 22 16.92z"/></svg>112</strong><span>Emergency · in case of acute danger to life</span></a>
                </div>
                <p class="krise-lead">All contact points at a glance:</p>
                <ul class="rd-faq-ul">
                  <li><strong>Emergency number 112</strong> (ambulance service, free of charge): for acute danger to life, after a suicide attempt, or when you or others are in acute danger.</li>
                  <li><strong>Emergency room of the responsible hospital</strong>: In acute mental health crises, you can go to the emergency room of a responsible hospital at any time, without an appointment. An overview of the hospitals obliged to admit patients in Mitte is available from the <a href="https://www.berlin.de/ba-mitte/politik-und-verwaltung/service-und-organisationseinheiten/qualitaetsentwicklung-planung-und-koordination-des-oeffentlichen-gesundheitsdienstes/psychiatriekoordination/klinische-versorgung-von-psychisch-kranken-erwachsenen-sowie-psychisch-kranken-kindern-und-jugendlichen-in-berlin-mitte-821617.php" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Mitte District Office (Bezirksamt Mitte)</a>.</li>
                  <li><strong>Berliner Krisendienst (Berlin Crisis Service)</strong>: free of charge, anonymous on request, available by phone around the clock and, in urgent cases, with a home visit. Phone <a href="tel:+49303906310">030 390 63 10</a> (for Mitte and Friedrichshain-Kreuzberg; at night, on weekends and on public holidays, this number connects you to the Berlin emergency service). Numbers for the other districts are at <a href="https://www.berliner-krisendienst.de/ich-brauche-hilfe/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">berliner-krisendienst.de</a>.</li>
                  <li><strong>Medical on-call service 116 117</strong>: outside practice opening hours, when symptoms cannot wait until the next day but there is no acute danger to life.</li>
                  <li><strong>TelefonSeelsorge</strong> (telephone counseling): free of charge, anonymous and around the clock at <a href="tel:08001110111">0800 111 0 111</a>, <a href="tel:08001110222">0800 111 0 222</a> or <a href="tel:116123">116 123</a>. Also by chat or email via <a href="https://www.telefonseelsorge.de/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">telefonseelsorge.de</a>.</li>
                  <li><strong>krisenchat</strong> (for people under 25): free of charge and around the clock by chat via WhatsApp or SMS, when writing is easier than speaking. More information at <a href="https://www.krisenchat.de/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">krisenchat.de</a>.</li>
                  <li><strong>Your GP's office, a psychiatric or psychotherapeutic practice, or the Social Psychiatric Service (Sozialpsychiatrischer Dienst) of your district</strong>: during the day, when the situation is not acutely life-threatening. Contact details for the Social Psychiatric Service are on your district office's website.</li>
                </ul>
                <p>Further information is available from the <a href="https://gesund.bund.de/wege-im-gesundheitswesen/erwachsenenleben/psychische-gesundheit/anlaufstellen-bei-psychischen-krisen" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Federal Health Portal (Gesundheitsportal des Bundes)</a>.</p></div></div>
            </div>
            <div class="rd-faq-item">
              <button class="rd-faq-q" aria-expanded="false"><span class="rd-num">07</span><span class="rd-q">Is everything we discuss kept confidential, and what does the duty of confidentiality mean?</span><span class="faq-toggle"></span></button>
              <div class="rd-faq-a"><div class="rd-faq-a-inner"><p>Your personal data and everything discussed in counseling or therapy are subject to a legal duty of confidentiality. Without your express written consent, I do not share any information with third parties. This duty can be lifted only in a few legally defined situations, namely when you or others are in acute danger to life or limb.</p><p>For quality assurance, I receive supervision of my own work and take part in teaching supervision in training contexts. I always present cases anonymously there, meaning no personal data is passed on.</p></div></div>
            </div>
            <div class="rd-faq-item">
              <button class="rd-faq-q" aria-expanded="false"><span class="rd-num">08</span><span class="rd-q">Am I welcome regardless of relationship form, gender identity and sexual orientation?</span><span class="faq-toggle"></span></button>
              <div class="rd-faq-a"><div class="rd-faq-a-inner"><p>Yes. Everyone is welcome. Gender identities and sexual orientations are diverse, and relationships and families take many forms: as a couple, in a multi-partner relationship or as a family.</p><p>In my work, what matters most is how the people involved can shape contact, understanding and connection with one another.</p></div></div>
            </div>
            <div class="rd-faq-item">
              <button class="rd-faq-q" aria-expanded="false"><span class="rd-num">09</span><span class="rd-q">What does &ldquo;systemic&rdquo; mean in therapy and counseling?</span><span class="faq-toggle"></span></button>
              <div class="rd-faq-a"><div class="rd-faq-a-inner"><p>Systemic work looks at people in their relationships and contexts and focuses on strengths and solutions. You can read more about this above, in the section <a href="#arbeitsverstaendnis">&ldquo;My professional perspective&rdquo;</a>.</p></div></div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="rd-faq-detail" aria-live="polite"><div class="rd-faq-detail-bar"></div><div class="rd-faq-detail-body"></div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

